<BaseLayout title="About"><section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-24"><p class="kicker">About / Boyuan (Ben) Wang</p><h1 class="text-4xl mt-6 mb-8">Mechanical engineering, with robots in mind.</h1><div class="prose"><p>I’m a mechanical engineering M.S. student at Duke, graduating in December 2026, and a graduate researcher in the General Robotics Lab. I earned my B.S. in Mechanical Engineering at Ohio State, with a minor in Computer and Information Science.</p><p>My strongest work is in hardware: mechanisms, manufacturing, actuation, assembly, and troubleshooting. I use simulation and code to support that work, from kinematic models and robot configuration search to motor control and experiment infrastructure.</p><p>Long term, I want to build practical robots that help people with everyday physical tasks, particularly in elder care.</p><h2>Tools I work with</h2><p>SolidWorks, Fusion, GD&amp;T, Python, C++, URDF, PyBullet, MuJoCo, ROS / ROS 2, machining, rapid prototyping, soldering, and electromechanical system integration.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p><a href="mailto:bw277@duke.edu">bw277@duke.edu</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/boyuan-ben-wang/">LinkedIn</a></p></div></section></BaseLayout>
